\contentsline {table}{\numberline {6.8}{\ignorespaces Average and Max particle rates per $cm^2$ for specified checkpoints along the length of the detector. The particle rates are collected not from the geometrical acceptance of the corresponding sub-detectors but from the cross section of the outer volume for the sub-detector found in the Monte Carlo. For the Straw-1\&3 a circle of radius of 141.5\,mm, NCHOD a square of length 330\,mm, CHOD a square of length 244\,mm, IRC a square of length 122\,mm, MEC a circle of radius 182.5\,mm, MUV-1\&2 a square of length 320\,mm, MUV-3 a square of length 281\,mm and HAC a square of length 281\,mm. A geometrical cut has been made to remove particles that pass though the checkpoints within the expected beam dispersion radius calculated to be $0.4\times 10^{-3}\times Z$, where Z is the position of the checkpoint.}}{128}{table.caption.95}%
